  "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'our insurance' as the focal point of the meme's message. The phrase 'our insurance' implies a collective or group identity (the KKK individuals) that is being metaphorically equated with a financial safety net, and the user is invited to interpret this as a cynical or satirical commentary on the group's reliance on or profiting from insurance. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the possessive 'our' creates an implicit projection of the user as part of the group being referenced, or as an observer interpreting the group's 'insurance' as a darkly humorous or critical concept.",
